@startuml
title ER Diagram - Recruitment Marketing (HubSpot objects)

hide methods
hide stereotypes

' --- Core HubSpot objects (conceptual ERD) ---

entity "Company" as Company {
  * company_id : string <<PK>>  ' TODO: actual HubSpot object id field
  --
  name : string
  ' TODO: portal access / permissions model (not provided)
}

entity "JobVacancy" as Vacancy {
  * vacancy_id : string <<PK>>  ' 
  --
  reference_id : string <<FK>>       ' internal reference id
  content_available : boolean   '
  requirements_available : boolean
  lifecycle_state : string      '
  meta_campaign_live : boolean  ' 
}

entity "Contact (candidate)" as Candidate {
  * candidate_id : string <<PK>> '
  --
  created_at : datetime
}

entity "Lead" as Lead {
  * lead_id : string <<PK>> '
  --
  created_at : datetime
  status : string      
  vacancy_id : string <<FK>>  ' link to JobVacancy (not enforced in HubSpot)
  candidate_id : string <<FK>> ' link to Contact (candidate)
}


entity "LeadForm" as LeadForm {
  * lead_form_id : string <<PK>> ' Meta lead form id
  --
  source : string                ' expected: Meta
  name : string
}

' --- Relationships (based on the requirements) ---

Company ||--o{ Vacancy

Vacancy ||--|| LeadForm
Candidate }o--|| LeadForm

Vacancy ||--o{ Lead : "has leads"
Lead }o--|| Candidate : "references contact"
Lead }o--|| Company

note on link
Contact (candidate) is not directly associated
to JobVacancy. The association runs through Lead:
JobVacancy -> Lead -> Contact (candidate).
end note

note right of Vacancy
Lifecycle states:
- Content_Available
- Requirements_Available
- Deal_Won
- Campaign_Live
- Campaign_Closed
end note

note right of Lead
Status values:
- New
- Attempting
- Connected,
- Sending_Documents
- Qualified_By_Us,
- Approved_By_Customer
- Rejected
end note

note left of LeadForm
Created/managed in Meta (Facebook Lead Forms),
linked to Vacancy via HubSpot workflow.
end note

@enduml
